cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "CoarseDeGiorgi: a Lean 4 formalization of local boundedness and Harnack inequalities under coarse ellipticity"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of local boundedness above
  for weak subsolutions, and of the weak Harnack and Harnack inequalities for
  nonnegative weak supersolutions and solutions, of divergence-form elliptic
  equations with symmetric, possibly degenerate and unbounded coefficients in
  dimension d >= 3. The hypothesis bounds two coarse ellipticity constants,
  discounted spatial moments of two coarse-grained matrices of the
  coefficient field on the simplices of triadic triangulations; it holds in
  the moment range of Bella and Schäffner and under a Besov-type
  negative-regularity condition on the coefficients and their inverses.
  Explicit examples, also formalized, show that this condition is sharp in its
  whole range and that the powers of the coarse ellipticity ratio in
  the local bound are optimal. Built on the public CoarseGraining library. The
  library contains no sorry and no custom axiom; each Mathlib-only comparator
  challenge contains one intentional statement-level sorry, checked against
  its completed solution.
type: software
